{
  "info": {
    "name": "Taskflow API",
    "description": "Covers Project + Task CRUD, validation failures, 404 handling, cross-project ownership checks, pagination/filtering, and the four Task query techniques (JOIN FETCH-backed list, JPQL status-counts, native ILIKE search, projection summary).\n\nPrerequisites:\n- The app must be running (`./mvnw spring-boot:run`), Docker up for the Postgres compose service.\n- Two users must already exist in the DB (there's no registration endpoint yet - Day 9). Seed them once with:\n  `docker exec -it demo-postgres-1 psql -U taskflow -d taskflow -c \"INSERT INTO users (username, email, password_hash) VALUES ('postman.alice','postman.alice@example.com','placeholder'), ('postman.bob','postman.bob@example.com','placeholder') RETURNING id, username;\"`\n  and set the `ownerId` / `otherOwnerId` collection variables to the returned ids (defaults below assume ids 2 and 3).\n\nRun the whole collection top to bottom (Collection Runner) - later requests depend on ids captured by earlier ones via test scripts.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8080" },
    { "key": "ownerId", "value": "2" },
    { "key": "otherOwnerId", "value": "3" },
    { "key": "projectId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "secondProjectId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "taskId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "searchTaskId", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 - Projects",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create Project (valid)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/projects",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Taskflow API\",\n  \"description\": \"Build the REST layer\",\n  \"ownerId\": {{ownerId}}\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            }
          },
          "event": [{
            "listen": "test",
            "script": {
              "type": "text/javascript",
              "exec": [
                "pm.test(\"Status code is 201\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                "pm.test(\"Location header present\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get(\"Location\")).to.include(\"/api/projects/\"));",
                "const json = pm.response.json();",
                "pm.test(\"Response has generated id\", () => pm.expect(json.id).to.be.a(\"number\"));",
                "pm.test(\"ownerId echoed\", () => pm.expect(json.ownerId).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"ownerId\") * 1));",
                "pm.test(\"taskCount is 0 for a new project\", () => pm.expect(json.taskCount).to.eql(0));",
                "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"projectId\", json.id);"
              ]
            }
          }]
        },
        {
          "name": "Create Second Project (for cross-project tests)",
